#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114933 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbb56f0a-ead0-5794-9e33-7fe0e1f87dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cosecant Function"}] :question/id #uuid "118a33c0-5831-586e-a0a5-e8bd3e1e4c9a" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3644" :question/problem "Find $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = 2 \\csc x$." :question/worked-solution "Here, we just take the constant out of the derivative and use the result for the derivative of $\\csc x$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2\\csc x) \\\\\n&= 2\\frac{d}{dx}(\\csc x) \\\\\n&= 2(-\\csc x\\cot x) \\\\\n&=-2\\csc x\\cot x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114934 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9699341b-c4e2-547f-8d98-bcda30567272" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cotangent Function"}] :question/id #uuid "23b1cfcf-9f46-5274-b07b-66770a827409" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3646" :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac {\\textrm d y} {\\textrm d x}$ if $y = 2x - 3\\cot x$." :question/worked-solution "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(2x - 3\\cot x) \\\\\n&= 2 - 3(-\\csc^{2} x) \\\\\n&= 2 + 3\\csc^{2} x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114935 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4b3974-1288-524e-a34c-8091c0e072f1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Secant Function"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2548d6-87fc-56b1-aa7d-cef328eb4e24" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3647" :question/problem "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = x\\sec x$." :question/worked-solution "We use the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x\\sec x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(x) \\cdot \\sec x + x \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sec x) \\\\\n&= (1) \\cdot \\sec x + x \\cdot (\\sec x\\tan x) \\\\\n&= \\sec x(1 + x\\tan x)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114936 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7995b377-1de4-5126-aa29-8cc30b4918f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent at a Point of a Function Involving Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "83b8a6dd-c8c4-5537-ac88-289265752755" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-3648" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$ if $f(x) = \\dfrac{-2\\cot x}{\\sin x}$." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative using the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{-2\\cot x}{\\sin x}) \\\\\n&= (\\frac{d}{dx}(-2\\cot x) \\cdot \\sin x - (-2\\cot x) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\sin x))/([\\sin x]^{2}) \\\\\n&= (-2(-\\csc^{2} x) \\cdot \\sin x + 2\\cot x \\cdot (\\cos x))/(\\sin^{2} x) \\\\\n&= \\frac{2\\csc x + 2\\cot x\\cos x}{\\sin^{2} x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nin the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(\\frac{π}{4}) &= (2\\csc (\\frac{π}{4}) + 2\\cot (\\frac{π}{4})\\cos (\\frac{π}{4}))/(\\sin^{2} (\\frac{π}{4})) \\\\\n&= (2 \\cdot (\\sqrt{2}) + 2 \\cdot (1) \\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}))/((\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})^{2}) \\\\\n&= (3\\sqrt{2})/((\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 6\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e4b3974-1288-524e-a34c-8091c0e072f1" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Secant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e17abfbb-5844-5bdc-80bf-86703a1b3e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+1)}{3{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248283} {:answer/id #uuid "9c632c13-bc85-5531-9998-b3556be6b133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248284} {:answer/id #uuid "2540fa54-b3ca-5ce0-91fe-65612532407b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(3-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248285} {:answer/id #uuid "a755b304-0fb7-56a8-8232-2903c230c934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1)}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248286} {:answer/id #uuid "565a8e84-07dd-5d35-94ed-6dafbdb33858" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1)}{{e}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a755b304-0fb7-56a8-8232-2903c230c934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x-1)}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248286} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d379418-78d1-5002-9b9f-c53c2fb31b13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248282}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b368b0a-0220-5cfb-93f5-8a417e2e96fc" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104325" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{3sec⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3sec⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3sec⁡xtan⁡x)({e}^{x})-(3sec⁡x)({e}^{x})}{({e}^{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{x}sec⁡x(tan⁡x-1)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3sec⁡x(tan⁡x-1)}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7995b377-1de4-5126-aa29-8cc30b4918f8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Slope of the Tangent at a Point of a Function Involving Reciprocal Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4eed6e5-eae5-5e6b-801a-b25c696c2cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248290} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf19b6c-af92-5d90-bcd1-8078b0ad20f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248291} {:answer/id #uuid "36517077-3145-59b3-b2af-bc2ba33d330b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248292} {:answer/id #uuid "5858c024-44a6-55dc-807c-3b31aa22a22f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248293} {:answer/id #uuid "9c58ab88-5b11-5129-8a45-ef2705f61378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36517077-3145-59b3-b2af-bc2ba33d330b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248292} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a0d3914-f422-5228-818f-9386cc9c4aff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248289}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "166ab305-d740-5b5f-8db8-e4dc0cbb781b" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-104442" :question/problem "Find the slope of $y=f(x)$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ if $f(x)=\\frac{sec⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\pi }.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{sec⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{sec⁡xtan⁡x}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\frac{6x}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ in the derivative and get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{\\pi /3} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot sec⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\cdot tan⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{6}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}+2 \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248295 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbb56f0a-ead0-5794-9e33-7fe0e1f87dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daacc65a-5e8d-5439-8749-4207676e0203" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248297} {:answer/id #uuid "dacb83f6-6faf-522c-8e58-34a2c9461f13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248298} {:answer/id #uuid "aa17aceb-3f32-59c6-bbf6-9f5ea5b86981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248299} {:answer/id #uuid "4e6c67a4-9d16-5ff0-a360-6319d37406d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248300} {:answer/id #uuid "509de197-28ee-5d5a-a2d5-ea3bfa1556dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e6c67a4-9d16-5ff0-a360-6319d37406d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248300} :answer-field/id #uuid "5848f73e-6a5d-5454-b5ca-1f19912d7ecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248296}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "760a6beb-1c0b-5274-bb23-84beaeb824a7" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-105298" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ if $f(x)=ln⁡x-5csc⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x-5csc⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}-5(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}+5csc⁡xcot⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ in the derivative and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}+5csc⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})cot⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }+5\\cdot 1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbb56f0a-ead0-5794-9e33-7fe0e1f87dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7e91844-248e-5809-aa65-409d71626870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248304} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0be612-d93c-5992-8885-5f1d9728fef4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248305} {:answer/id #uuid "2f94eff4-ad11-5f48-8a9d-77f6ba7d6c7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248306} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a3580b-6bcb-5431-9270-274a54f06c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x({2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248307} {:answer/id #uuid "bc88fae1-84aa-51b8-99e6-9bb1a2410a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc88fae1-84aa-51b8-99e6-9bb1a2410a77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248308} :answer-field/id #uuid "7723083b-417e-5b5a-ac24-b958be334814" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "191f4c6b-bf0a-5363-8304-95a5223cc0b0" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-105299" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)={2}^{x}csc⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "We calculate the derivative using the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}csc⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}ln⁡2(csc⁡x)+{2}^{x}(-csc⁡xcot⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}csc⁡x(ln⁡2-cot⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186248309 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9699341b-c4e2-547f-8d98-bcda30567272" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Expressions Involving the Cotangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e221412-b8b4-567a-a075-681e1894003a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248311} {:answer/id #uuid "b810b47b-2c5d-5379-ac34-01ef740fe52d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248312} {:answer/id #uuid "749fe71b-27bd-510d-8ec4-f85a25927e5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248313} {:answer/id #uuid "e44d670c-1bef-55c1-9b56-142d649802d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{5}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248314} {:answer/id #uuid "242e462a-b292-5742-bb1c-9b990bb54fa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/valu